    "text": "# Engineering Handbook: Incident Response for AquaCore Control Systems (ACCS)\n\n**Document ID:** ACCS-IR-2024-01\n**Version:** 3.2\n**Classification:** Internal Engineering / Critical Infrastructure\n**Applicability:** All AquaCore Control Service (ACCS) Field Engineers, SCADA Administrators, and Network Security Operations Center (NSOC) Staff.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Introduction and Scope\n\n### 1.1 Purpose\nThis handbook defines the standardized procedures for detecting, analyzing, containing, and recovering from incidents affecting the AquaCore Control Service (ACCS). ACCS manages the Supervisory Control and Data Acquisition (SCADA) systems for municipal water treatment plants, including chemical dosing, filtration control, and distribution pressure management.\n\n### 1.2 Criticality\nWater treatment systems are classified as **Critical Infrastructure**. Incidents may result in:\n*   **Public Health Risks:** Under-dosing of chlorine, contamination, or turbidity spikes.\n*   **Physical Damage:** Pump cavitation, pipe bursts due to pressure surges.\n*   **Regulatory Violations:** Failure to meet EPA/Local Water Authority standards.\n\n### 1.3 Incident Severity Levels",
